# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
service-account*.json

# NOT ignored, deliberately: google-services.json / GoogleService-Info.plist.
#
# Firebase *client* config is an identifier, not a credential. It ships inside
# every APK and anyone can extract it in a minute; Google's own guidance says
# so. Security comes from App Check, Auth rules and Storage/Firestore rules —
# never from hiding this file.
#
# Grouping it with service-account*.json and *.key, which ARE private keys, did
# two bad things at once: it implied a protection that does not exist, and it
# broke a fresh clone, because `lib/firebase_options.dart` is committed, is
# imported by main(), and carries the very same values. Ignoring one and
# committing the other protected nothing and cost the build.
#
# If a real server key ever lands here, it goes above this comment.

